# The chat model for Diya on a 16 GB computer: the same weights as qwen3:4b-instruct, with the context capped.
#
# qwen3:4b-instruct asks Ollama for a 262,144-token context window by default, and its cache for that is about 39 GB, so on 16 GB it fails to
# load. Diya cannot pass num_ctx through Ollama's OpenAI-style endpoint, so the cap is made here, once:
#
#     ollama pull qwen3:4b-instruct
#     ollama create diya-chat -f ollama/diya-chat.Modelfile
#     (then set DIYA_MODEL=diya-chat)
#
# 16,384 tokens is a 2.4 GB cache and is the value that was measured (docs/MODEL_BENCHMARK.md). It shares the weights, so nothing more is downloaded.
FROM qwen3:4b-instruct
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384
